0..74 Comment "/// Two transports of one value compare when one value is a call\'s result."
75..78 Comment "///"
79..155 Comment "/// The lowering binds a call\'s result before the transport runs. The kernel"
156..231 Comment "/// runs that call before it reads the path, so a comparison meets the call"
232..242 Comment "/// first."
243..246 Comment "///"
247..325 Comment "/// Each row transports a value along a variable path, and a call that returns"
326..400 Comment "/// the value along the same path. The families are a loop and a path to a"
401..417 Comment "/// fixed point."
418..421 Comment "///"
422..521 Comment "/// - see: #3806 — the checker compared the transports first, and the kernel refused its dialogue"
523..591 Comment "/// A definition that returns its argument, so a call to it unfolds."
